## 5.3 Product display system

Every product must be showcased professionally.

Use a consistent product card system with:

1. Properly framed product image.
2. Brand.
3. Readable product title.
4. Variant, weight or pack size.
5. Actual price in PKR.
6. Original price when discounted.
7. Clear discount information.
8. Product availability.
9. Add to Cart.
10. Wishlist.
11. Quick View only when useful.

### Product photography standards

- Use authentic product images wherever possible.
- Do not distort product packaging.
- Preserve actual product logos.
- Preserve product color and shape.
- Avoid cropping important package details.
- Use consistent image containers.
- Prefer a neutral background for product packshots.
- Apply subtle framing instead of heavy shadows.
- Avoid stretching low-resolution product images.
- Maintain proper object-fit behavior.
- Use appropriate image ratios for apparel and other nonstandard products.

Product image containers should remain visually consistent while allowing different product types to display correctly.

### Product grid

Create professionally balanced layouts:

- Wide desktop: 4–5 columns when card width permits.
- Standard desktop: 3–4 columns.
- Tablet: 2–3 columns.
- Mobile: 2 columns when readable, otherwise a single comfortable column.

Never sacrifice readability merely to display more products.

Product titles, prices and cart controls must remain aligned.

## 5.4 Discount design

Make offers visually appealing but credible.

Discount presentation should include:

- Current sale price.
- Original price with strikethrough.
- Percentage or amount saved when meaningful.
- An understated discount label.
- Campaign terms when relevant.

Calculate the discount correctly:

Discount % = ((Original Price - Sale Price) / Original Price) × 100.

Never invent a discount.

Do not display a false percentage or misleading savings.

Use a restrained and consistent discount color.

Avoid flashy badges on every product.

## 5.5 Product hover and quick actions

Hover interactions may include:

- Subtle image emphasis.
- Wishlist.
- Quick View.
- Add to Cart.

Keep motion subtle.

Do not rearrange the entire card on hover.

Touch devices must expose equivalent actions without requiring hover.

